  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nThe upper ridge gradually shifts east into the weekend, shutting\ndown the precip chances and triggering another warming trend with \nhighs returning to the upper 90s to mid 100s by the weekend and \ninto next week. While temperatures will be above normal, the heat \nis not forecast to be quite as dramatic as what we experienced \nthis past week, owing to the center of the ridge continuing east \ntowards the mid-Tennessee Valley. \n\nWith that upper ridge centered well to the east, and the storm\ntrack focused across the north-central Plains, several days of \nsouth or southwest sfc flow will be present locally. Disturbances \nmay occasionally track close enough to the area to offer some low \nprecip chances throughout next week, however, there is enough \nmodel spread at this stage that the blended guidance keeps PoPs \nbelow 20% each day Mon-Wed.",
